1
00:00:00,800 --> 00:00:08,250
Her SIM card stopped working on Tuesday. She replaced it. By
Friday, that routine change blocked her checkout.

2
00:00:08,760 --> 00:00:16,171
Here, cash on delivery is most of e-commerce. A fake order
costs a merchant a real van and a real driver.

3
00:00:16,596 --> 00:00:26,620
So merchants use a rule. SIM changed recently: decline. It is
cheap, and it is wrong. Most people who replace a SIM lost a
phone.

4
00:00:27,342 --> 00:00:36,409
Generative A.I. has broken every soft proof that someone is
genuine. Deepfakes pass liveness. Voice clones defeat call
centres.

5
00:00:36,833 --> 00:00:45,639
The one thing a model cannot fake is a physical SIM, in radio
range of a real cell tower, with years of history behind it.

6
00:00:46,064 --> 00:00:51,814
CAMARA is the first time that truth has been programmable by
anyone outside the operator.

7
00:00:52,536 --> 00:00:59,743
Isnad treats a SIM change as the start of an investigation,
not the end of a customer relationship.

8
00:01:00,168 --> 00:01:08,593
The name is literal. Isnad is the classical chain of
transmission: judging a report by scrutinising every link that
carried it.

9
00:01:09,018 --> 00:01:15,350
Human, SIM, device, location, history. Each link a CAMARA
call, each shown with its own source.

10
00:01:16,073 --> 00:01:23,119
Here is the checkout. Fifteen hundred dollars, cash on
delivery, a new account, and a SIM replaced this week.

11
00:01:23,501 --> 00:01:29,600
The agent buys number verification first: cheapest useful
check. The network number matches.

12
00:01:29,982 --> 00:01:40,004
Then SIM swap. It comes back adverse, and it stays in the
chain. The operator change date is a separate row, because it
is a second billable call.

13
00:01:40,387 --> 00:01:46,714
Device swap: the handset is unchanged. Location: she is where
she said. Same person, new SIM.

14
00:01:47,139 --> 00:01:57,260
Challenge, not decline. Policy score zero point three two two,
between the thresholds on screen. The merchant asks one more
question instead of losing her.

15
00:01:57,982 --> 00:02:03,347
Every decision is signed. The receipt proves this instance
issued exactly these bytes.

16
00:02:03,729 --> 00:02:08,828
Change one word and verification fails, offline, with no call
back to us.

17
00:02:09,210 --> 00:02:16,627
What it does not prove is that the operator told the truth. A
signed mock receipt is still mock, and the page says so.

18
00:02:17,349 --> 00:02:21,077
Now with Gemini choosing. Watch who is speaking on each row.

19
00:02:21,418 --> 00:02:33,274
The model opens with SIM swap, in its own words. One adverse
signal cannot carry a decline, so policy demands
corroboration. The trace says policy, not model.

20
00:02:33,699 --> 00:02:40,257
Then the model says stop, and policy overrules it to buy the
cheapest check that could still resolve the doubt.

21
00:02:40,683 --> 00:02:46,102
The model chooses what to buy. Policy decides what it means,
and what may not be skipped.

22
00:02:46,824 --> 00:02:55,558
Eight CAMARA APIs on Nokia Network as Code. Fourteen recorded
calls to Nokia's hosted simulator, failures included.

23
00:02:55,940 --> 00:03:08,091
On a thirteen-case evaluation, Isnad spends forty-nine
provider operations where a run-everything pipeline spends
seventy-eight. At pennies per call, that gap is the business
model.

24
00:03:08,473 --> 00:03:13,096
One thousand three hundred and ten automated tests, English
and Arabic.

25
00:03:13,819 --> 00:03:21,324
What we have not proven: no physical handset has completed a
consent round trip, and the risk score is uncalibrated.

26
00:03:21,748 --> 00:03:28,176
We name those, because an engine whose whole argument is
provenance does not get to be vague about its own.

27
00:03:28,899 --> 00:03:33,837
Clone it, run make setup and make judge, and every number here
is one command away.

28
00:03:34,219 --> 00:03:38,930
The internet never got its isnad. Every verdict this engine
issues is one.
